 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Food preparation is making food ready to eat: cleaning, cutting, mixing and cooking.\nMethods of cooking: boiling, steaming (bobolo, koki), frying, roasting or grilling (soya, roasted plantain and corn), baking (bread), stewing.\nImportance of cooking:\n• kills germs and parasites (in meat, fish, eggs);\n• softens food so it is easier to chew and digest;\n• improves taste and smell;\n• removes some poisons (cassava, some beans).\nGood habits: wash hands; wash fruit and vegetables in clean water; cook meat well; do not overcook vegetables (vitamins are lost) — steam or cook them for a short time; keep cooked food covered; do not reuse frying oil many times.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "v": "green vegetables"
  },
  "problem": "Why should {v} not be boiled for a long time?",
  "steps": [
   "Some vitamins (like vitamin C) are destroyed by long heating.",
   "They also dissolve into the water, which is thrown away."
  ],
  "answer": "Long boiling destroys and washes out the vitamins.",
  "checks": []
